---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

// Plain-language privacy policy. Every statement here describes how the site
// actually runs; when the deployment changes (deploy/, the Caddyfile, a new
// third-party service), this page changes with it. The effective date is the
// date of the last substantive edit.
const EFFECTIVE = "November 10, 2026";
---

<Base
	title="Privacy — Chino Valley Today"
	description="What Chino Valley Today collects about readers (almost nothing), what our hosting providers see, and how to reach us."
>
	<header class="legalhead">
		<div class="shell legalhead__inner">
			<h1 class="legalhead__title">Privacy</h1>
			<p class="legalhead__date mark">Effective {EFFECTIVE}</p>
		</div>
	</header>

	<div class="reading body prose">
		<p>
			Chino Valley Today is a local news site about Chino and Chino Hills. It
			does not track its readers. This page explains what information is
			collected when you use the site and who collects it.
		</p>

		<h2>The short version</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>No accounts, no sign-up, no newsletter list.</li>
			<li>No analytics, advertising, or tracking scripts, and no cookies of our own.</li>
			<li>
				Our web server and our network provider, Cloudflare, handle technical
				request data such as IP addresses.
			</li>
			<li>If you email us, we keep your message and address so we can reply.</li>
			<li>We do not sell personal information or share it for advertising.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>When you read the site</h2>
		<p>
			Pages are plain HTML. Nearly every page ships no script at all, and the
			fonts are served from our own server, so reading a page contacts only us
			and our network provider.
		</p>
		<p>
			Our web server can log each request: the page, the time, what your
			browser reports about itself (its user agent), and the network address
			the request came from. Requests reach us through Cloudflare, so that
			address is usually Cloudflare's, though the log may also include your IP
			address as Cloudflare passes it along. We use these logs only to keep the
			site running and to investigate abuse. They sit in the server's system
			log, which deletes old entries automatically.
		</p>
		<p>
			Traffic reaches us through Cloudflare, which provides the site's
			encryption and protects it from attacks. To do that, Cloudflare processes
			the same request information, including your IP address, and shows us
			traffic totals. It may also set a strictly necessary security cookie when
			it needs to check that a request is not an attack. Its handling is
			described in the
			<a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener noreferrer"
				>Cloudflare privacy policy</a
			>.
		</p>
		<p>
			The RSS feed and podcast episodes are ordinary files on the same server,
			and requests for them are handled the same way. Your feed reader or
			podcast app has its own privacy practices.
		</p>

		<h2>When you email us</h2>
		<p>
			Mail to <a href="mailto:corrections@chinovalley.today"
				>corrections@chinovalley.today</a
			> is forwarded by Cloudflare Email Routing to the editor's inbox, which
			is hosted by a third-party email provider. We use your message and
			address to answer you and to make any correction you report. We do not
			add you to any list, and we will not publish your name or message
			without your permission.
		</p>

		<h2>Third-party content you choose to play</h2>
		<p>
			Some pages may feature a video hosted by a social platform, such as
			TikTok. Nothing from that platform loads until you press play. When you
			do, the video plays in the platform's own player, and the platform's
			privacy policy applies to that player, including any cookies it sets.
			Other sites we link to have their own privacy policies.
		</p>

		<h2>People named in the record</h2>
		<p>
			The site reports from public records: agendas, minutes, meeting video,
			licence reports, and agency releases. Those records sometimes name
			people. Our editorial rules restrict naming private individuals and do
			not allow naming minors. The <a href="/about/">About</a> page describes
			how those items are reviewed. To ask about an item that names you, email
			the address above.
		</p>

		<h2>Children</h2>
		<p>
			The site is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly
			collect personal information from them.
		</p>

		<h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
		<p>
			You can read the whole site without an account and without giving us
			your name or email address. If you have emailed us and want that
			correspondence deleted, or want to know what we hold about you, email the
			address above. We aim to answer within 30 days. The California Consumer
			Privacy Act applies to businesses larger than this site, but we will
			still act on a request to see or delete your information, wherever you
			live. We do not sell or share personal information as that law defines
			those terms.
		</p>

		<h2>Changes</h2>
		<p>
			When this policy changes, the effective date at the top changes with it.
			A change that collects more about readers will be explained on this page
			before it takes effect.
		</p>
	</div>
</Base>

<style>
	.legalhead {
		background: var(--crate);
		color: #fff;
		border-bottom: 6px solid var(--placard);
	}
	.legalhead__inner {
		padding-block: 1.9rem 2.2rem;
		max-width: 44rem;
	}
	.legalhead__title {
		margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
		font-size: clamp(1.55rem, 1.2rem + 2vw, 2.5rem);
		line-height: 1.16;
		font-weight: 600;
	}
	.legalhead__date {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: 0.78rem;
	}
	.body {
		padding-block: 2.4rem 1rem;
	}
</style>
